<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The daily job, owned by launchd instead of by the Next server.

  WHY THIS EXISTS. The in-process timer is registered at server boot and its closure holds the
  module graph from that moment, so a code change after boot is invisible to it. That shipped a
  stale digest on two consecutive mornings while the correct code sat committed on disk. A process
  started per run reads the code as it is, every time — which is the whole fix.

  RunAtLoad is false on purpose: loading this agent should not fire a Plaid sync and an email at
  whatever moment it happens to be installed.

  BACKUP FIRST, AND WITH `;` RATHER THAN `&&`. The backup runs before the sync so the dump captures
  the database as it stood before the day's mutations — if a sync corrupts something, last night's
  dump is from before it. The separator is a semicolon so a failed backup does not cancel the sync,
  the snapshot and the mail: those are three independent jobs and a backup problem should cost
  exactly one of them. The backup's own exit code is in the log either way.

  Only runs while the machine is awake and the user is logged in. launchd will run a missed job
  once shortly after wake, which the in-process timer never did — but a laptop closed all day still
  misses that day. Moving this to the always-on server is Phase 2 step 19.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.b8.daily-job</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <!-- A login shell, so nvm/homebrew node is on PATH exactly as it is in a terminal. launchd's
         own PATH is minimal and would not find node at all. -->
    <string>cd __APP_DIR__ &amp;&amp; npm run backup; exec npm run job:daily</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__APP_DIR__/ops/daily-job.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__APP_DIR__/ops/daily-job.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
